              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} Matrix theory
              approach of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"} Banks
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Willy+Fischler"} Fischler
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+Susskind"} Susskind
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
              of modes in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
              multiplet in 11-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+space"} Minkowski space
              \- even at energies sufficiently large that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
              should be created. (This latter phenomenon has never been explicitly demonstrated). But Matrix theory is only a beginning and does not give us the whole picture of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              If history is a good guide, then we should expect that anything as profound and far-reaching as a fully satisfactory formulation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              is surely going to lead to new and novel mathematics. Regrettably, it is a problem the community seems to have put aside - temporarily. But, ultimately, Physical Mathematics must return to this grand issue.
          %p
